{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself."}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization"},"metadata":{"title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"your own","type":"text"}]},{"text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"text":" and add a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift"},{"text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","text":"Overriding text per-app"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", mirroring ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" from the SwiftUI side.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenStateContainerView","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenStateStore","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the person using the app."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"topic","title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","abstract":[{"text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announcement.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateView","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Renders the right content for a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", switching between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithUIKit":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithuikit","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a UIKit screen’s four states with ","type":"te